From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:47:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: eliza: reserve the rest of the DARE regions

The Eliza boot firmware protects two DDR regions for the hypervisor
and TZ, 0x80000000-0x81960000 and 0xd8000000-0xdb800000; neither is OS
memory. eliza.dtsi reserves only their first parts (gunyah-hyp,
cpusys-vm and cpucp up to 0x81300000, tz-merged up to 0xd8600000), and
leaves 0x81300000-0x81960000, which holds the hypervisor tag storage,
and 0xd8600000-0xdb800000 undescribed.

U-Boot takes the DDR banks from SMEM and the reservations from the
device tree, so it maps both ranges as RAM and hands them to the OS.

Reserve both as no-map in a U-Boot device tree fragment shared by the
MTP and the CQS EVK, until the Linux eliza.dtsi describes them and that
reaches dts/upstream. This protects the OS only when it boots with
U-Boot's device tree: a DTB loaded from the ESP needs the same nodes.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
